# Pit Scout environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development (`cp .env.example .env.local`) and fill in
# the values. `.env.local` is git-ignored; never commit real values. For Vercel, set the
# same variables in Project Settings > Environment Variables (Production AND Preview).
#
# Variables prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time:
# they are public, so only put values here that are safe to expose. Changing one
# requires a redeploy/rebuild. Everything else is server-only and never reaches the browser.
#
# There is deliberately NO Supabase service-role key. The app does not need it.
# Never add one, and never give a secret a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

# --- Supabase (PUBLIC, browser-visible) ---------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL.
#  - Local: run `npx supabase start`, then use the "API URL" it prints (http://127.0.0.1:54321).
#  - Hosted: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API > Project URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase publishable (formerly "anon") key. Safe to expose; access is enforced by
# row level security, and every policy requires a signed-in user.
#  - Local: `npx supabase status` prints it ("Publishable" key).
#  - Hosted: dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys > Publishable key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Legacy name for the same key (the "anon" JWT key). Only used when
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is unset. Leave commented out unless you
# have to use the legacy key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- The Blue Alliance (SERVER-ONLY, secret) -----------------------------------------

# TBA Read API key, sent as the X-TBA-Auth-Key header from route handlers only
# (src/lib/env.server.ts imports `server-only`, so it cannot leak to the client).
# Get one at https://www.thebluealliance.com/account > "Read API Keys" > Add New Key.
TBA_API_KEY=

# --- Optional / tests only ----------------------------------------------------------

# `npm run test:live` runs the opt-in live TBA + Statbotics integration test. It sets
# LIVE=1 itself and reads TBA_API_KEY from `.env.local` directly. Nothing to configure here.
